# Line-ending policy, committed so it applies to everyone rather than living in
# each machine's core.autocrlf.
#
# text=auto lets git decide text vs binary per file and normalizes text to LF in
# the repository. The working tree then follows the platform, so a Windows
# checkout is CRLF and a clone elsewhere is LF - both store the same bytes.
* text=auto

# Images are content, not text - never let git touch their bytes.
*.png binary
